# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Audio is a BUILD ARTEFACT, not source.
#
# audio/ holds ~6,200 MP3s (~102 MB) generated from Google Translate's
# translate_tts endpoint, which is undocumented and not licensed for
# redistribution. Committing it would be republication, and git remembers a
# file even after you delete it — so it has to be excluded before the first
# commit, not cleaned up afterwards.
#
# Regenerate with:
#   python tools/extract_strings.py
#   python tools/fetch_audio.py tools/ro-strings.json
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
audio/
audio-manifest.js

# Intermediate output of the audio pipeline. Regenerated by extract_strings.py,
# so there is nothing to preserve — and ro-strings.json has been written to both
# the root and tools/ at different times, hence both patterns.
ro-strings.json
tools/ro-strings.json
tools/failed.json
tools/verb-report.json
tools/*.log

# Screenshots captured while reporting bugs during development. Useful in the
# moment, not project history.
*.png
*.jpg

# Third-party exam papers and books downloaded for reference. Someone else's
# copyright; keep them local.
tools/ilr/
*.pdf

# Local tool configuration — may contain machine paths and granted permissions.
# launch.json is kept: it is how anyone runs the project.
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock

# OS and editor noise
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store
*.swp
*~
.vscode/
.idea/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
